  "dcterms:title": "SMART Trust demonstrator: journeys J1 to J4",
  "schema:numberOfItems": 163,
  "schema:hasPart": [
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.BirthClinicSystem",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.BirthClinicSystem",
      "dcterms:title": "Birth clinic issuing system",
      "schema:name": "BirthClinicSystem",
      "dcterms:description": "The hospital system abroad that issues a DVC per dose with the HCERT library: the HCERT issuing system (smart-trust-tools) of a trust network participant (XXR).\n\n**Persona**: Software that calls the library once per dose and never holds the private key; signs only with a DSC its country's CSCA issued and has already shared with the GDHCN.\n\n**Also known as**: Issuer of the birth-dose DVCs (SMART Trust Issuer)\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- Kesaro Provincial Hospital system, Taifafeki (Country A, XXR)\n\n**In the user scenarios**:\n\n- [J1 — Born abroad](scenarios.html#j1--born-abroad-taifafeki-birth-day): J1 An Onesan baby is born in Taifafeki\n\n**On the device screens**: [S1 Birth Abroad & Printed DVC QR Cards (Dr. Anan's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S1/)\n\n**Discussed in the workshop modules**: [M1 From journey to capabilities](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m1/); [M4 Trust, credentials and wallets](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m4/); [M5 Governance, decision rights and the legal basis](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m5/)\n\n**Lanes and tasks in the business processes**:\n\n- [J1 Issue the newborn's birth-dose DVCs in Country A](business-processes.html#j1-issue-the-newborns-birth-dose-dvcs-in-country-a): Build one DVCMinPreQual payload per dose; Prepare: CWT claims and the COSE Sig_structure; Finish: COSE_Sign1, deflate, Base45, HC1:\n\n**Data sets its tasks record or read**: [TD.J1 Birth-dose DVC](dictionary.html#tdj1-birth-dose-dvc)",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.BirthClinicSystem"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.BirthClinicSystem.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.BirthClinicVaccinator",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.BirthClinicVaccinator",
      "dcterms:title": "Birth clinic vaccinator",
      "schema:name": "BirthClinicVaccinator",
      "dcterms:description": "The clinician abroad who gives the birth doses and hands over the signed paper DVC (J1).\n\n**Persona**: A maternity-ward clinician who records doses in the hospital system and prints what it produces.\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- ![Dr. Anan](data:image/svg+xml;base64,) [Dr. Anan](personas.html#dr-anan-taifafeki-clinician--birth--follow-up-taifafeki), Dr Anan (clinician, Kesaro, Taifafeki)\n\n**In the user scenarios**:\n\n- [J1 — Born abroad](scenarios.html#j1--born-abroad-taifafeki-birth-day): J1 An Onesan baby is born in Taifafeki (told through Dr. Anan)\n\n**On the device screens**: [S1 Birth Abroad & Printed DVC QR Cards (Dr. Anan's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S1/); [S8 Foreign Clinic VHL Viewer & Audit Trace (Dr. Anan's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S8/)\n\n**Discussed in the workshop modules**: [M1 From journey to capabilities](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m1/); [M4 Trust, credentials and wallets](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m4/); [M5 Governance, decision rights and the legal basis](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m5/)\n\n**User stories** ([all stories](scenarios.html#user-stories)):\n\n- I want to print a signed record of each birth dose the family can carry anywhere\n\n**Lanes and tasks in the business processes**:\n\n- [J1 Issue the newborn's birth-dose DVCs in Country A](business-processes.html#j1-issue-the-newborns-birth-dose-dvcs-in-country-a): Give Hep B and BCG birth doses and record them; Print the paper DVC, one QR per dose",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.BirthClinicVaccinator"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.BirthClinicVaccinator.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.Caregiver",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.Caregiver",
      "dcterms:title": "Caregiver",
      "dcterms:description": "The parent who holds the child's paper DVCs and the family phone, and presents them; IHE ITI VHL VHL Holder and smart-trust Holder.\n\n**Persona**: A parent carrying a newborn's records across borders on paper and one shared phone; no health training, little time, limited connectivity.\n\n**Also known as**: VHL Holder (IHE ITI VHL); Holder (SMART Trust)\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- ![Bounmy](data:image/svg+xml;base64,) [Bounmy](personas.html#bounmy-father--holds-the-family-phone-onesa), Bounmy SENGMANY (father, holds the family phone)\n- ![Khamla](data:image/svg+xml;base64,) [Khamla](personas.html#khamla-mother-onesa), Khamla SENGMANY (mother)\n\n**In the user scenarios**:\n\n- [J1 — Born abroad](scenarios.html#j1--born-abroad-taifafeki-birth-day): J1 An Onesan baby is born in Taifafeki\n- [J2 — Found at home](scenarios.html#j2--found-at-home-onesa-3-weeks-later): J2a A health worker finds the baby — and reads his cards; J2b Registered at home, and referred\n- [J3 — Made official](scenarios.html#j3--made-official-lomaru-district-health-center-4-weeks-later): J3a The clinic confirms the cards are genuine; J3b Taifafeki vaccines are fitted to the Onesan schedule\n- [J4.0 — Crossing back: one family, one phone](scenarios.html#j40--crossing-back-one-family-one-phone-onesa-12-months-later): J4.0a One phone holds the whole family’s records (told through Bounmy); J4.0b Dad creates a link to share at the clinic (told through Bounmy)\n- [J4.1 — Crossing back: a Taifafeki doctor sees the full history](scenarios.html#j41--crossing-back-a-taifafeki-doctor-sees-the-full-history-kesaro-12-months-later): J4.1 A Taifafeki doctor sees the full history\n\n**On the device screens**: [S1 Birth Abroad & Printed DVC QR Cards (Dr. Anan's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S1/); [S2 Offline QR Scan of the Foreign Cards (Vilay's phone)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S2/); [S3 Newborn Registration & Clinic Referral (Vilay's phone)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S3/); [S4 Clinic Referral & GDHCN Verification (Chanthason's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S4/); [S5 Terminology Adjudication & National Schedule (Chanthason's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S5/); [S6 One Family, One Phone Household Wallet (Bounmy's phone)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S6/); [S7 VHL QR Display & Passcode Protection (Bounmy's phone)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S7/); [S8 Foreign Clinic VHL Viewer & Audit Trace (Dr. Anan's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S8/)\n\n**Discussed in the workshop modules**: [M1 From journey to capabilities](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m1/); [M2 The reference architecture and where you stand](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m2/); [M3 Standards, specifications and the core data set](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m3/); [M4 Trust, credentials and wallets](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m4/); [M5 Governance, decision rights and the legal basis](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m5/); [M6 Doing it once, together](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m6/); [M7 Our first move, what it costs, and what we ask for](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m7/)\n\n**User stories** ([all stories](scenarios.html#user-stories)):\n\n- I want to have my son's birth doses from abroad recognised at home, so that his care does not start over and nothing is repeated\n- I want to show each family member's records abroad from our one shared phone, with a passcode I can say aloud, so that a doctor abroad can treat us without paper or an app\n- I want to decide who sees my child's record, and for how long, so that the record stays at home and I know who has looked\n\n**Lanes and tasks in the business processes**:\n\n- [J1 Issue the newborn's birth-dose DVCs in Country A](business-processes.html#j1-issue-the-newborns-birth-dose-dvcs-in-country-a): its lane holds no task\n- [J2 Discover and refer an unregistered infant in Country B](business-processes.html#j2-discover-and-refer-an-unregistered-infant-in-country-b): Show the paper DVCs from Country A\n- [J3 Verify, import and schedule at the home clinic](business-processes.html#j3-verify-import-and-schedule-at-the-home-clinic): its lane holds no task\n- [J4.0 Issue the family's records to one phone as VHLs](business-processes.html#j40-issue-the-familys-records-to-one-phone-as-vhls): Choose who to share, with a passcode and an expiry\n- [J4.1 Read a family member's records at the point of care abroad](business-processes.html#j41-read-a-family-members-records-at-the-point-of-care-abroad): its lane holds no task",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.Caregiver"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.Caregiver.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.ChwApp",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.ChwApp",
      "dcterms:title": "CHW app",
      "schema:name": "ChwApp",
      "dcterms:description": "The OHS app on the CHW's phone: reads a foreign DVC without verifying it (triage read, STT-VER-011), registers the child and records a referral, all offline, syncing later.\n\n**Persona**: Offline-first Android app; must never present an unverified record as verified.\n\n**Also known as**: Triage reader (SMART Trust Receiver, read-unverified)\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- CHW app, Onesa (Country B)\n\n**In the user scenarios**:\n\n- [J2 — Found at home](scenarios.html#j2--found-at-home-onesa-3-weeks-later): J2a A health worker finds the baby — and reads his cards; J2b Registered at home, and referred\n\n**On the device screens**: [S2 Offline QR Scan of the Foreign Cards (Vilay's phone)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S2/); [S3 Newborn Registration & Clinic Referral (Vilay's phone)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S3/)\n\n**Discussed in the workshop modules**: [M2 The reference architecture and where you stand](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m2/); [M3 Standards, specifications and the core data set](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m3/); [M4 Trust, credentials and wallets](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m4/); [M5 Governance, decision rights and the legal basis](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m5/)\n\n**Lanes and tasks in the business processes**:\n\n- [J2 Discover and refer an unregistered infant in Country B](business-processes.html#j2-discover-and-refer-an-unregistered-infant-in-country-b): Read each DVC unverified (triage); Add the infant; save doses as reported; Create a referral to the home clinic for verification\n\n**Decisions it makes**:\n\n- Decision table [TD.DT.01 What does a scanned DVC become in the child's record?](decision-logic.html#tddt01-what-does-a-scanned-dvc-become-in-the-childs-record), in: Read each DVC unverified (triage); Add the infant; save doses as reported\n\n**Data sets its tasks record or read**: [TD.J2A Newborn registration on a home visit](dictionary.html#tdj2a-newborn-registration-on-a-home-visit); [TD.J2B Referral for verification](dictionary.html#tdj2b-referral-for-verification)\n\n**Indicators that count its decisions**: [TD.IND.01 Foreign doses imported as verified](indicators.html#tdind01-foreign-doses-imported-as-verified); [TD.IND.03 CHW referrals for verification completed at the clinic](indicators.html#tdind03-chw-referrals-for-verification-completed-at-the-clinic)",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.ChwApp"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.ChwApp.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.CommunityHealthWorker",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.CommunityHealthWorker",
      "dcterms:title": "Community health worker",
      "schema:name": "CommunityHealthWorker",
      "dcterms:description": "Finds unregistered children on home visits, registers them and refers them to the clinic (J2).\n\n**Persona**: Works on foot and offline, on a cheap Android phone; registers and refers, never judges authenticity.\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- ![Vilay](data:image/svg+xml;base64,) [Vilay](personas.html#vilay-community-health-worker--village-04-onesa), Vilay (community health worker, Village 04, Onesa)\n\n**In the user scenarios**:\n\n- [J2 — Found at home](scenarios.html#j2--found-at-home-onesa-3-weeks-later): J2a A health worker finds the baby — and reads his cards (told through Vilay); J2b Registered at home, and referred (told through Vilay)\n\n**On the device screens**: [S2 Offline QR Scan of the Foreign Cards (Vilay's phone)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S2/); [S3 Newborn Registration & Clinic Referral (Vilay's phone)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S3/)\n\n**Discussed in the workshop modules**: [M2 The reference architecture and where you stand](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m2/); [M3 Standards, specifications and the core data set](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m3/); [M4 Trust, credentials and wallets](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m4/); [M5 Governance, decision rights and the legal basis](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m5/)\n\n**User stories** ([all stories](scenarios.html#user-stories)):\n\n- I want to read a foreign vaccination QR offline and register the child with it, so that the clinic sees what was given before the family arrives\n- I want to refer a child whose foreign record needs checking, so that verification is done by someone who can\n- I want to register a newborn into the household offline, before civil registration, so that no newborn in my village is missed, even with no signal\n\n**Lanes and tasks in the business processes**:\n\n- [J2 Discover and refer an unregistered infant in Country B](business-processes.html#j2-discover-and-refer-an-unregistered-infant-in-country-b): Scan each QR with the CHW app; Explain the referral to the family",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.CommunityHealthWorker"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.CommunityHealthWorker.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.FamilyPhone",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.FamilyPhone",
      "dcterms:title": "Family phone",
      "schema:name": "FamilyPhone",
      "dcterms:description": "The one smartphone the family shares, holding one VHL QR per member (J4); holds links, not keys to anyone's records beyond what each link grants.\n\n**Persona**: A shared Android phone, sometimes offline; whoever holds it can show any member's QR, the passcode protects the records.\n\n**Also known as**: Personal health wallet\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- The family's shared phone\n\n**In the user scenarios**:\n\n- [J4.0 — Crossing back: one family, one phone](scenarios.html#j40--crossing-back-one-family-one-phone-onesa-12-months-later): J4.0b Dad creates a link to share at the clinic\n- [J4.1 — Crossing back: a Taifafeki doctor sees the full history](scenarios.html#j41--crossing-back-a-taifafeki-doctor-sees-the-full-history-kesaro-12-months-later): J4.1 A Taifafeki doctor sees the full history\n\n**On the device screens**: [S7 VHL QR Display & Passcode Protection (Bounmy's phone)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S7/); [S8 Foreign Clinic VHL Viewer & Audit Trace (Dr. Anan's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S8/)\n\n**Discussed in the workshop modules**: [M5 Governance, decision rights and the legal basis](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m5/); [M6 Doing it once, together](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m6/); [M7 Our first move, what it costs, and what we ask for](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m7/)\n\n**Lanes and tasks in the business processes**:\n\n- [J4.0 Issue the family's records to one phone as VHLs](business-processes.html#j40-issue-the-familys-records-to-one-phone-as-vhls): Store each member's VHL QR on the phone\n- [J4.1 Read a family member's records at the point of care abroad](business-processes.html#j41-read-a-family-members-records-at-the-point-of-care-abroad): Show the child's VHL QR",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.FamilyPhone"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.FamilyPhone.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.GdhcnTrustAnchor",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.GdhcnTrustAnchor",
      "dcterms:title": "GDHCN trust anchor",
      "schema:name": "GdhcnTrustAnchor",
      "dcterms:description": "WHO's GDHCN, which receives participants' PKI material and distributes it as DID trust lists; Trust Network Anchor (SMART Trust), Trust Anchor (IHE ITI VHL).\n\n**Persona**: A WHO service publishing DID documents over did:web; verifiers fetch it when online and keep a copy.\n\n**Also known as**: Trust Network Anchor (SMART Trust); Trust Anchor (IHE ITI VHL)\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- GDHCN DEV trust network (WHO)",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.GdhcnTrustAnchor"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.GdhcnTrustAnchor.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.HomeClinicEhr",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.HomeClinicEhr",
      "dcterms:title": "Home clinic EHR",
      "schema:name": "HomeClinicEhr",
      "dcterms:description": "The clinic's OHS-based record system: verifies DVCs against the GDHCN trust list, imports them as FHIR Immunization resources and evaluates the national schedule (J3).\n\n**Persona**: Holds the DID trust list from its last refresh, about weekly for a clinic without its own connection, when the CHW visits the base clinic or district health office; loading it is a precondition of a visit, and it verifies offline at the point of care.\n\n**Also known as**: Verifier at the home clinic (SMART Trust Receiver)\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- Lomaru District Health Center EHR (Country B)\n\n**In the user scenarios**:\n\n- [J3 — Made official](scenarios.html#j3--made-official-lomaru-district-health-center-4-weeks-later): J3a The clinic confirms the cards are genuine; J3b Taifafeki vaccines are fitted to the Onesan schedule\n\n**On the device screens**: [S4 Clinic Referral & GDHCN Verification (Chanthason's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S4/); [S5 Terminology Adjudication & National Schedule (Chanthason's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S5/)\n\n**Discussed in the workshop modules**: [M1 From journey to capabilities](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m1/); [M3 Standards, specifications and the core data set](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m3/); [M4 Trust, credentials and wallets](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m4/); [M6 Doing it once, together](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m6/)\n\n**Lanes and tasks in the business processes**:\n\n- [J3 Verify, import and schedule at the home clinic](business-processes.html#j3-verify-import-and-schedule-at-the-home-clinic): Verify each HCERT against the trust list; Import the doses as FHIR Immunization resources; Add national codes beside foreign ones; Evaluate the national schedule\n\n**Decisions it makes**:\n\n- Decision table [TD.DT.01 What does a scanned DVC become in the child's record?](decision-logic.html#tddt01-what-does-a-scanned-dvc-become-in-the-childs-record), in: Verify each HCERT against the trust list; Every DVC verified?; Import the doses as FHIR Immunization resources\n- Decision table [TD.DT.02 Which national schedule code does an imported dose carry?](decision-logic.html#tddt02-which-national-schedule-code-does-an-imported-dose-carry), in: Add national codes beside foreign ones\n- Decision table [TD.DT.03 Does the national schedule count this dose?](decision-logic.html#tddt03-does-the-national-schedule-count-this-dose), in: Evaluate the national schedule\n- Decision table [TD.DT.04 Is this dose of the national schedule due?](decision-logic.html#tddt04-is-this-dose-of-the-national-schedule-due), in: Evaluate the national schedule\n- Gateway \"Every DVC verified?\" in [J3 Verify, import and schedule at the home clinic](business-processes.html#j3-verify-import-and-schedule-at-the-home-clinic)\n\n**Data sets its tasks record or read**: [TD.J3A DVC verification and import](dictionary.html#tdj3a-dvc-verification-and-import); [TD.J3B Imported dose and schedule](dictionary.html#tdj3b-imported-dose-and-schedule)\n\n**Indicators that count its decisions**: [TD.IND.01 Foreign doses imported as verified](indicators.html#tdind01-foreign-doses-imported-as-verified); [TD.IND.03 CHW referrals for verification completed at the clinic](indicators.html#tdind03-chw-referrals-for-verification-completed-at-the-clinic); [TD.IND.04 Imported doses carrying a national schedule code](indicators.html#tdind04-imported-doses-carrying-a-national-schedule-code)",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.HomeClinicEhr"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.HomeClinicEhr.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.HomeClinicProvider",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.HomeClinicProvider",
      "dcterms:title": "Home clinic provider",
      "schema:name": "HomeClinicProvider",
      "dcterms:description": "The nurse at the home clinic who receives the referral, has the foreign DVCs verified and decides catch-up doses (J3).\n\n**Persona**: Trusts the system's verdict and needs a reason when a certificate fails.\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- ![Chanthason](data:image/svg+xml;base64,) [Chanthason](personas.html#chanthason-nurse--district-health-center-onesa), Nurse Chanthason (Lomaru District Health Center, Onesa)\n\n**In the user scenarios**:\n\n- [J3 — Made official](scenarios.html#j3--made-official-lomaru-district-health-center-4-weeks-later): J3a The clinic confirms the cards are genuine (told through Chanthason); J3b Taifafeki vaccines are fitted to the Onesan schedule (told through Chanthason)\n\n**On the device screens**: [S4 Clinic Referral & GDHCN Verification (Chanthason's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S4/); [S5 Terminology Adjudication & National Schedule (Chanthason's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S5/)\n\n**Discussed in the workshop modules**: [M1 From journey to capabilities](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m1/); [M3 Standards, specifications and the core data set](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m3/); [M4 Trust, credentials and wallets](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m4/); [M6 Doing it once, together](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m6/)\n\n**User stories** ([all stories](scenarios.html#user-stories)):\n\n- I want to know whether a foreign certificate is genuine, and why not when it is not\n- I want to see which doses are due once the foreign doses are imported, so that I give only what is missing\n- I want to keep the foreign vaccine code and add our schedule code beside it, deciding myself when there is no match, so that the other country's record is never overwritten and the next nurse need not decide again\n\n**Lanes and tasks in the business processes**:\n\n- [J3 Verify, import and schedule at the home clinic](business-processes.html#j3-verify-import-and-schedule-at-the-home-clinic): Scan the QRs and open the referral; Note the failure; decide doses by policy; Give due doses and book the next visit\n\n**Decisions it makes**:\n\n- Decision table [TD.DT.01 What does a scanned DVC become in the child's record?](decision-logic.html#tddt01-what-does-a-scanned-dvc-become-in-the-childs-record), in: Note the failure; decide doses by policy\n- Decision table [TD.DT.04 Is this dose of the national schedule due?](decision-logic.html#tddt04-is-this-dose-of-the-national-schedule-due), in: Give due doses and book the next visit\n\n**Data sets its tasks record or read**: [TD.J2B Referral for verification](dictionary.html#tdj2b-referral-for-verification); [TD.J3A DVC verification and import](dictionary.html#tdj3a-dvc-verification-and-import); [TD.J3B Imported dose and schedule](dictionary.html#tdj3b-imported-dose-and-schedule)\n\n**Indicators that count its decisions**: [TD.IND.01 Foreign doses imported as verified](indicators.html#tdind01-foreign-doses-imported-as-verified); [TD.IND.03 CHW referrals for verification completed at the clinic](indicators.html#tdind03-chw-referrals-for-verification-completed-at-the-clinic)",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.HomeClinicProvider"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.HomeClinicProvider.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.IssuerKey",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.IssuerKey",
      "dcterms:title": "Issuer signing key",
      "schema:name": "IssuerKey",
      "dcterms:description": "The DSC private key of the issuing participant, in an HSM, cloud KMS or Android Keystore; signs the bytes the issuing system prepares (two-phase signing, STT-ISS-004).\n\n**Persona**: A key that signs what it is given and reveals nothing else.\n\n**Also known as**: Document signer (DSC) key\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- XXR document signer key (Country A, Taifafeki)\n\n**In the user scenarios**:\n\n- [J1 — Born abroad](scenarios.html#j1--born-abroad-taifafeki-birth-day): J1 An Onesan baby is born in Taifafeki\n- [J4.0 — Crossing back: one family, one phone](scenarios.html#j40--crossing-back-one-family-one-phone-onesa-12-months-later): J4.0b Dad creates a link to share at the clinic\n\n**On the device screens**: [S1 Birth Abroad & Printed DVC QR Cards (Dr. Anan's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S1/); [S7 VHL QR Display & Passcode Protection (Bounmy's phone)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S7/)\n\n**Discussed in the workshop modules**: [M1 From journey to capabilities](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m1/); [M4 Trust, credentials and wallets](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m4/); [M5 Governance, decision rights and the legal basis](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m5/); [M6 Doing it once, together](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m6/)\n\n**Lanes and tasks in the business processes**:\n\n- [J1 Issue the newborn's birth-dose DVCs in Country A](business-processes.html#j1-issue-the-newborns-birth-dose-dvcs-in-country-a): Sign the bytes with XXR's DSC key\n- [J4.0 Issue the family's records to one phone as VHLs](business-processes.html#j40-issue-the-familys-records-to-one-phone-as-vhls): Sign with Country B's DSC key\n\n**Data sets its tasks record or read**: [TD.J1 Birth-dose DVC](dictionary.html#tdj1-birth-dose-dvc)",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.IssuerKey"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.IssuerKey.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.NationalPortal",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.NationalPortal",
      "dcterms:title": "National health portal",
      "schema:name": "NationalPortal",
      "dcterms:description": "The home country's portal that issues each family member's records (IPS, DVCs) as a passcode-protected Verifiable Health Link and hosts the manifests (J4.0), checking the passcode, expiry and consent on each request and logging every access at home (J4.1): the VHL Sharer.\n\n**Persona**: A government service signing with the national DSC, issued under the national CSCA and already shared with the GDHCN; hosts manifests and encrypted documents for a limited time.\n\n**Also known as**: VHL Sharer (IHE ITI VHL); Issuer of the family's VHLs (SMART Trust Issuer)\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- Onesa national health portal and gateway (Country B, XXK)\n\n**In the user scenarios**:\n\n- [J4.0 — Crossing back: one family, one phone](scenarios.html#j40--crossing-back-one-family-one-phone-onesa-12-months-later): J4.0b Dad creates a link to share at the clinic\n- [J4.1 — Crossing back: a Taifafeki doctor sees the full history](scenarios.html#j41--crossing-back-a-taifafeki-doctor-sees-the-full-history-kesaro-12-months-later): J4.1 A Taifafeki doctor sees the full history\n\n**On the device screens**: [S7 VHL QR Display & Passcode Protection (Bounmy's phone)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S7/); [S8 Foreign Clinic VHL Viewer & Audit Trace (Dr. Anan's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S8/)\n\n**Discussed in the workshop modules**: [M5 Governance, decision rights and the legal basis](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m5/); [M6 Doing it once, together](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m6/); [M7 Our first move, what it costs, and what we ask for](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m7/)\n\n**Lanes and tasks in the business processes**:\n\n- [J4.0 Issue the family's records to one phone as VHLs](business-processes.html#j40-issue-the-familys-records-to-one-phone-as-vhls): Assemble each member's IPS and DVCs; Encrypt, publish a passcode manifest; Prepare the HCERT carrying the VHL at key 5; Finish the HC1 QR text\n- [J4.1 Read a family member's records at the point of care abroad](business-processes.html#j41-read-a-family-members-records-at-the-point-of-care-abroad): Check passcode, log access, return manifest\n\n**Decisions it makes**:\n\n- Decision table [TD.DT.05 Does the portal release the manifest for this request?](decision-logic.html#tddt05-does-the-portal-release-the-manifest-for-this-request), in: Check passcode, log access, return manifest\n\n**Data sets its tasks record or read**: [TD.J40 Shared link and consent](dictionary.html#tdj40-shared-link-and-consent); [TD.J41 Access to a shared link](dictionary.html#tdj41-access-to-a-shared-link)\n\n**Indicators that count its decisions**: [TD.IND.02 Shared-link openings that were authorised](indicators.html#tdind02-shared-link-openings-that-were-authorised)",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.NationalPortal"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.NationalPortal.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.PocProvider",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.PocProvider",
      "dcterms:title": "Point-of-care provider",
      "schema:name": "PocProvider",
      "dcterms:description": "The clinician abroad who scans the family's QR and reads the child's records (J4.1).\n\n**Persona**: Has minutes, no prior relationship with the family, and her own hospital's system.\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- ![Dr. Anan](data:image/svg+xml;base64,) [Dr. Anan](personas.html#dr-anan-taifafeki-clinician--birth--follow-up-taifafeki), Dr Anan (clinician, Kesaro, Taifafeki)\n\n**In the user scenarios**:\n\n- [J4.1 — Crossing back: a Taifafeki doctor sees the full history](scenarios.html#j41--crossing-back-a-taifafeki-doctor-sees-the-full-history-kesaro-12-months-later): J4.1 A Taifafeki doctor sees the full history (told through Dr. Anan)\n\n**On the device screens**: [S1 Birth Abroad & Printed DVC QR Cards (Dr. Anan's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S1/); [S8 Foreign Clinic VHL Viewer & Audit Trace (Dr. Anan's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S8/)\n\n**Discussed in the workshop modules**: [M5 Governance, decision rights and the legal basis](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m5/); [M6 Doing it once, together](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m6/); [M7 Our first move, what it costs, and what we ask for](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m7/)\n\n**User stories** ([all stories](scenarios.html#user-stories)):\n\n- I want to read a visiting child's summary and vaccinations from a QR the parent shows, so that without installing anything or calling another country\n- I want to know the record I read abroad came from the child's home country and was not altered, so that I can rely on it as I would on my own clinic's record\n\n**Lanes and tasks in the business processes**:\n\n- [J4.1 Read a family member's records at the point of care abroad](business-processes.html#j41-read-a-family-members-records-at-the-point-of-care-abroad): Scan the QR and enter the passcode the caregiver says; Not verified: treat records as paper; Review history, allergies and vaccinations\n\n**Decisions it makes**:\n\n- Decision table [TD.DT.06 Does the receiver follow the VHL?](decision-logic.html#tddt06-does-the-receiver-follow-the-vhl), in: Not verified: treat records as paper",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.PocProvider"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.PocProvider.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.PocReceiver",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.PocReceiver",
      "dcterms:title": "Point-of-care receiver",
      "schema:name": "PocReceiver",
      "dcterms:description": "The clinic system abroad that scans a VHL, verifies it, fetches the manifest (ITI-YY5) and decrypts the documents (J4.1): the VHL Receiver.\n\n**Persona**: A hospital system on a trust network with its own receiver key; its DID trust list is a cache refreshed nightly or hourly, loaded before a visit, so it verifies without being online.\n\n**Also known as**: VHL Receiver (IHE ITI VHL); Receiver of the family's VHLs (SMART Trust Receiver)\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- Kesaro primary care clinic viewer, Taifafeki (J4.1)\n\n**In the user scenarios**:\n\n- [J4.1 — Crossing back: a Taifafeki doctor sees the full history](scenarios.html#j41--crossing-back-a-taifafeki-doctor-sees-the-full-history-kesaro-12-months-later): J4.1 A Taifafeki doctor sees the full history\n\n**On the device screens**: [S8 Foreign Clinic VHL Viewer & Audit Trace (Dr. Anan's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S8/)\n\n**Discussed in the workshop modules**: [M5 Governance, decision rights and the legal basis](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m5/); [M6 Doing it once, together](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m6/); [M7 Our first move, what it costs, and what we ask for](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m7/)\n\n**Lanes and tasks in the business processes**:\n\n- [J4.1 Read a family member's records at the point of care abroad](business-processes.html#j41-read-a-family-members-records-at-the-point-of-care-abroad): Verify the HCERT and read the VHL at key 5; Request the manifest (ITI-YY5), signed; Decrypt the IPS and DVCs\n\n**Decisions it makes**:\n\n- Decision table [TD.DT.06 Does the receiver follow the VHL?](decision-logic.html#tddt06-does-the-receiver-follow-the-vhl), in: Verify the HCERT and read the VHL at key 5; HCERT verified?; Request the manifest (ITI-YY5), signed\n- Gateway \"HCERT verified?\" in [J4.1 Read a family member's records at the point of care abroad](business-processes.html#j41-read-a-family-members-records-at-the-point-of-care-abroad)\n\n**Data sets its tasks record or read**: [TD.J41 Access to a shared link](dictionary.html#tdj41-access-to-a-shared-link)",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.PocReceiver"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.PocReceiver.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.SubjectOfCare",
      "@type": "fhir:ActorDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.SubjectOfCare",
      "dcterms:title": "Subject of care",
      "schema:name": "SubjectOfCare",
      "dcterms:description": "The person the records are about: the child whose doses are given, signed, registered, verified and shared. Acts through the caregiver, holds no device and plays no lane in the journeys' processes.\n\n**Persona**: A newborn whose vaccination history must follow him across a border he cannot speak for.\n\n**Also known as**: Patient; Care recipient\n\n**Played in the journeys by** (fictional):\n\n- ![Somsak](data:image/svg+xml;base64,) [Somsak](personas.html#somsak-baby--the-record-follows-him-onesa), Somsak SENGMANY (newborn)\n\n**In the user scenarios**:\n\n- [J1 — Born abroad](scenarios.html#j1--born-abroad-taifafeki-birth-day): J1 An Onesan baby is born in Taifafeki\n- [J2 — Found at home](scenarios.html#j2--found-at-home-onesa-3-weeks-later): J2b Registered at home, and referred\n- [J4.1 — Crossing back: a Taifafeki doctor sees the full history](scenarios.html#j41--crossing-back-a-taifafeki-doctor-sees-the-full-history-kesaro-12-months-later): J4.1 A Taifafeki doctor sees the full history\n\n**On the device screens**: [S1 Birth Abroad & Printed DVC QR Cards (Dr. Anan's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S1/); [S3 Newborn Registration & Clinic Referral (Vilay's phone)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S3/); [S8 Foreign Clinic VHL Viewer & Audit Trace (Dr. Anan's tablet)](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/demo/S8/)\n\n**Discussed in the workshop modules**: [M1 From journey to capabilities](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m1/); [M2 The reference architecture and where you stand](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m2/); [M4 Trust, credentials and wallets](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m4/); [M5 Governance, decision rights and the legal basis](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m5/); [M6 Doing it once, together](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m6/); [M7 Our first move, what it costs, and what we ask for](en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/dpi-h-policy-track/m7/)",
      "dcterms:type": "Requirements: Actor Definitions",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ActorDefinition/TrustDemo.Role.SubjectOfCare"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../ActorDefinition-TrustDemo.Role.SubjectOfCare.json"
      }
    },
    {
