    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoDdVhlShare",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdVhlShare",
      "dcterms:title": "TD.J40 Shared link and consent",
      "dcterms:description": "What the home country records when the holder shares a family member's summary as a Verifiable Health Link (VHL): who may read what, for how long, and that a passcode protects it.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Logical Models",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdVhlShare"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDemoDdVhlShare.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaDvcVerification",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaDvcVerification",
      "dcterms:title": "Onesa: foreign DVC verified against the GDHCN trust list",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J3a. The district EHR verifies each Taifafeki DVC offline against its cached copy of the GDHCN trust list, then imports the dose. This record says so.\n\nWhy: a verified dose replaces a reported one, so the record must show who verified what, against which policy, and which reported doses it removes. Anyone who later doubts a dose can follow this record back to the signed certificate and the issuing country's key.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaDvcVerification"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaDvcVerification.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaHousehold",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaHousehold",
      "dcterms:title": "Onesa: household on the CHW's roster",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J2a. The CHW finds that a newborn is missing from the household roster and adds Somsak as a member.\n\nWhy: Onesan community health work is organized by household. The roster is how a CHW notices that a child is missing, and it is the unit the family phone shares under in J4 (one phone, three profiles).",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaHousehold"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaHousehold.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaImmunization",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaImmunization",
      "dcterms:title": "Onesa: dose on the national schedule",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J3 and after. These are the Taifafeki birth doses once the district clinic has verified them, and every dose given in Onesa.\n\nWhy: the Onesan schedule engine works on Onesan EPI codes, so each dose must carry one. A dose that came from abroad keeps the issuer's product code beside the Onesan one, added through the ConceptMap and confirmed by the nurse. Nothing the other country said is overwritten. A verified foreign dose is recorded from its primary source, the signing hospital, and its Provenance says how it was verified.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaImmunization"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaImmunization.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaPatient",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaPatient",
      "dcterms:title": "Onesa: child registered by the community health worker",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J2 onwards. Vilay registers Somsak on a home visit, and the same patient carries every Onesan record that follows: the verified Taifafeki doses, the Onesan doses and the summary shared in J4.\n\nWhy: a child born abroad is not in the Onesan civil registry yet. A temporary id lets the CHW, the district clinic and the national portal all refer to the same child until civil registration catches up. The parents are recorded as contacts, because they hold the paper cards and later the family's VHLs.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaPatient"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaPatient.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaReferral",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaReferral",
      "dcterms:title": "Onesa: CHW referral to verify foreign cards",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J2b. The CHW refers Somsak to the district health center to have his foreign cards verified and his doses fitted to the Onesan schedule.\n\nWhy: the CHW cannot verify a DVC on the phone, but the clinic can. The referral points at the reported doses it is about, so the clinic knows exactly what to check, and the CHW can see when it is done.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaReferral"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaReferral.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaRegistration",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaRegistration",
      "dcterms:title": "Onesa: newborn registration captured offline",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J2a. These are the CHW's answers on the newborn registration form, which the app renders with Structured Data Capture and saves with no signal.\n\nWhy: in Onesa the form is the configuration, not code. A ministry can change the questions without shipping a new app. The answers are kept so that the Patient and Group extracted from them can always be traced back to what was asked and who answered.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaRegistration"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaRegistration.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaReportedImmunization",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaReportedImmunization",
      "dcterms:title": "Onesa: foreign dose as reported (not yet verified)",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J2b. The CHW app reads each Taifafeki paper DVC offline without checking its signature, and saves the dose like this.\n\nWhy: a CHW phone may have no trust list and no signal, but the doses should not be lost. Recording them with primarySource false, the paper card as the report origin and the family named in the note keeps them visibly \"reported, not verified\". The schedule will not count them until a clinic verifies them (J3). Only the issuer's product code is present, because mapping to the Onesan schedule is a clinical step for later.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaReportedImmunization"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaReportedImmunization.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaVhlAccess",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaVhlAccess",
      "dcterms:title": "Onesa: every VHL access logged at home",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J4.1. The Onesan national gateway records each attempt by a clinic abroad to fetch a family member's VHL manifest, the refused ones included.\n\nWhy: the family shares a link, not a copy, and the data stays in Onesa. Logging every access at home, following IHE Basic Audit Log Patterns, is what lets the family and the ministry see who looked, from where and when. A wrong passcode is logged too.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoOnesaVhlAccess"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDemoOnesaVhlAccess.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoTaifafekiImmunization",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoTaifafekiImmunization",
      "dcterms:title": "Taifafeki: dose given at the birth hospital (DVC source)",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J1. Each birth dose (Hep B, BCG) that Dr Anan gives is recorded here first. The hospital then packs it into a Digital Vaccination Certificate (HCERT, signed with XXR's key) and prints it as a QR card.\n\nWhy: the DVC can only carry what this record holds. The vaccine product, date, lot, dose number and the administering organization are exactly the fields the HCERT certificate needs. They are required here so every printed card is complete. The product is coded from the WHO PreQual-style product list, because that is the code Onesa will later map to its own schedule (J3).",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoTaifafekiImmunization"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDemoTaifafekiImmunization.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoTaifafekiPatient",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoTaifafekiPatient",
      "dcterms:title": "Taifafeki: newborn at the birth hospital",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J1. Kesaro Provincial Hospital registers Somsak under its own hospital number on the day he is born.\n\nWhy: a baby born to Onesan parents in Taifafeki has no Taifafeki citizen id, so the hospital number is the only identifier the hospital can put behind the dose records it signs. The DVCs it prints carry the name and date of birth, not this number. The family's home country therefore cannot rely on any Taifafeki identifier, and links the doses to its own patient (see the Onesan patient profile).",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoTaifafekiPatient"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDemoTaifafekiPatient.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoTaifafekiVhlReceipt",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoTaifafekiVhlReceipt",
      "dcterms:title": "Taifafeki: record of a summary read through a VHL",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J4.1. The Kesaro clinic viewer keeps this record when it opens Somsak's patient summary through the Verifiable Health Link that his father shows.\n\nWhy: the Taifafeki clinic views the Onesan record and does not copy it into a Taifafeki registry. So the clinic keeps a note of what it saw, where it came from, and how it was verified: the VHL's signature against Onesa's key on the GDHCN trust list, the manifest fetch, and the passcode. The Onesan side keeps its own log of the same access (the Onesan audit profile).",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoTaifafekiVhlReceipt"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDemoTaifafekiVhlReceipt.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ValueSet-TrustDemoCodeMappingBasisVS",
      "@type": "fhir:ValueSet",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ValueSet/TrustDemoCodeMappingBasisVS",
      "dcterms:title": "How an imported dose got its national schedule code",
      "dcterms:description": "Every code of TrustDemoCodeMappingBasis.",
      "dcterms:type": "Terminology: Value Sets",
